    travelers: 'Our family; meeting our friends on December 30 and saying goodbye on the morning of December 31.',
    gettingThere: 'Both families arrive in Houston on December 30 and stay at the same hotel in Webster. Arrival times and transport details still need to be added. On December 31, our family drives south on I-45 to Galveston after Space Center Houston. On January 2, we drive north through Houston to Dallas. On January 3, we shop at Costco and an Asian supermarket before driving home to Fayetteville.',
    transport: 'Our family travels by car. Our friends arrange their own ride to IAH; we do not need to take them. Planning estimates: Webster hotel to Space Center, 15–20 minutes; Space Center to Galveston, 45–60 minutes; Tremont to Moody Gardens, 20–25 minutes; Galveston Hyatt to Moody Gardens, 10–15 minutes. Allow about 6–7 hours each for Galveston to Dallas and Dallas to Fayetteville, including meals and breaks. Check live navigation before each drive.',
    budget: 'All four hotel nights are booked. Allow extra for attraction tickets, meals, fuel and parking. The Tremont reservation lists overnight valet parking at $36 plus tax. Compare Moody Gardens daytime and holiday ticket bundles so we do not pay twice for the same attractions.',
    flights: 'Our friends have an international flight from IAH at about 3:00 PM on December 31. Aim to reach the airport by noon, at least three hours before departure. Confirm the exact flight time and allow extra time for traffic and any rental-car return. They will travel to the airport independently.',
    summary: 'Start with a reunion in Webster, then explore space and head to the coast! Spend New Year’s Eve in Galveston’s historic downtown, enjoy Moody Gardens and its holiday lights on New Year’s Day, and wake up near the beach. Finish with a stop in Dallas and shopping before the drive home.',
    places: 'Houston / Webster: Space Center Houston. Focus on the main exhibits; add a NASA Tram Tour only if tickets and timing work.\nGalveston: The Strand historic district, the harbor, The Tremont House and a walk along the Seawall.\nMoody Gardens: Aquarium Pyramid, Rainforest Pyramid and Holiday Lights Trail. ICE LAND or a movie is optional.\nDallas: Costco and one Asian supermarket, preferably near each other in North Dallas, Richardson or Plano. Choose stores and check Sunday opening hours before the trip.',
    itinerary: [
      'Day 1 · Wed, Dec 30|Hello, Houston! Both families arrive and check in at Platinum Inn & Suites Webster. Meet for dinner and relax. Arrival times are still to be confirmed, so we will not book extra attractions or drive back into downtown Houston.',
      'Day 2 · Thu, Dec 31|Space, then the seaside! After breakfast, check out and pack the car. Visit Space Center at its earliest opening time. Our friends should leave for IAH by about 10:00–10:30 AM, or earlier if their flight, traffic or car return requires it. If Space Center opens at 10:00 AM, they will have almost no time to visit; do not buy nonrefundable tickets for this short stop. Our family can keep exploring, eat lunch and leave around 1:00–1:30 PM. Allow 45–60 minutes on I-45 South to Galveston. Ask Tremont to hold our bags, explore The Strand and harbor, and check in from 4:00 PM. Enjoy dinner and a gentle New Year’s Eve walk.',
      'Day 3 · Fri, Jan 1|Happy New Year at Moody Gardens! Have breakfast and check out around 9:00–9:30 AM. We can ask the beachfront Hyatt to hold our bags before heading to the park at its confirmed opening time. Spend about 1.5–2 hours in the aquarium. After lunch and a break, explore the rainforest for about 1–1.5 hours, then choose ICE LAND or a movie if everyone has energy. Eat an early dinner and rest. From 5:30 PM, enjoy the Holiday Lights Trail for about 1–1.5 hours. Head to Hyatt around 7:00–8:00 PM. If we need a hotel break after 3:00 PM, first check whether our tickets allow re-entry.',
      'Day 4 · Sat, Jan 2|One more beach walk! Breakfast is planned for 7:30–8:30 AM, followed by a Seawall stroll, photos and a little sand play from 8:30–9:30 AM. Keep it short if it is windy or rainy. Check out around 10:00 AM and drive north on I-45 through Houston toward Dallas, following live navigation to Park Central. Allow 6–7 hours with lunch and breaks. Aim to arrive at Hyatt Place Dallas/Park Central around 4:00–5:00 PM; traffic may delay us. Eat nearby and rest. Save the main shopping for tomorrow.',
      'Day 5 · Sun, Jan 3|Shopping, then home! Have breakfast, pack and check out. Visit Costco and one Asian supermarket in the same area, using their confirmed Sunday hours. The supermarket can come first if it opens earlier. Buy chilled and frozen food last when possible, and bring a cooler. After lunch, aim to leave at 1:00–1:30 PM, preferably no later than 2:00 PM. Allow about 6–7 hours including breaks to reach Fayetteville around 7:00–9:00 PM. Check winter road conditions and shorten shopping if we run late.'
    ].join('\n'),
    aurora: 'December 30–31: Platinum Inn & Suites Webster, 520 W Bay Area Blvd, Webster. Accessible studio with two queen beds. The confirmation shows unusual check-in/check-out times; ask the hotel for the actual times.\nDecember 31–January 1: The Tremont House, 2300 Ship Mechanic Street, Galveston. Atrium Queen/Queen room, booked with a free-night award. Check-in: 4:00 PM; check-out: noon.\nJanuary 1–2: Hyatt Select Galveston – Beachfront, 5924 Seawall Blvd. Two queen beds with an accessible bathtub. Check-in: 3:00 PM; check-out: 11:00 AM.\nJanuary 2–3: Hyatt Place Dallas/Park Central, 12411 N Central Expressway. Two queen beds and a sofa bed. Check-in: 3:00 PM; check-out: noon.\nWhy this order? Enjoy historic downtown from Tremont on New Year’s Eve, then stay near the beach after Moody Gardens. Take a beach walk before heading north.',
    notes: 'Airport timing: A shared Space Center visit is only possible if opening hours and the airport schedule allow it. Dinner on December 30 and breakfast on December 31 are the main times together. If the timing does not work, say goodbye at the hotel and visit Space Center separately. Do not make a Tram Tour a must-do for our friends.\nHoliday tickets: Moody Gardens currently lists holiday events through January 2, 2027, with the Holiday Lights Trail from 5:30–10:00 PM. Confirm New Year’s Day attraction hours and showtimes before departure. The Holiday Evening Pass is valid only after 4:00 PM and does not cover a morning visit. Check ticket bundles, ICE LAND entry times and re-entry rules.\nNew Year’s Eve dinner: Book a restaurant near The Strand. Staying up until midnight is optional; fireworks or special celebrations are not part of the confirmed plan.\nBefore we go: Confirm Space Center hours for December 31 and any Tram Tour booking, our friends’ flight and car-return details, Webster hotel times, and Dallas store locations and Sunday hours.\nWeather backup: Shorten the beach walk in strong wind or rain. Keep indoor attractions and the historic district as alternatives. Check Oklahoma and Arkansas roads for winter weather on January 3. All activity times are plans, not confirmed reservations.',
    sources: 'Cover photo: Trace Hudson / Pexels, Galveston Pleasure Pier: https://www.pexels.com/photo/amusement-park-near-body-of-water-2386404/\nSpace Center hours: https://spacecenter.org/hours/\nNASA Tram Tours: https://spacecenter.org/exhibits-and-experiences/nasa-tram-tour/\nIAH holiday travel tips: https://www.fly2houston.com/iah/related-content/holiday-questions-answered/\nMoody Gardens holiday events: https://www.moodygardens.com/holiday-season\nMoody Gardens hours: https://www.moodygardens.com/visitor-info/hours\nThe Tremont House: https://www.thetremonthouse.com/\nHyatt Select Galveston: https://www.hyatt.com/hyatt-select/en-US/utxaa-hyatt-select-galveston-beachfront',
