    "places": "Phoenix / Tempe / Scottsdale: Dobbins Lookout; Phoenix Sunrise Hot Air Balloon; Musical Instrument Museum; optional Butterfly Wonderland; ASU Art Museum; Papago Park / Hole-in-the-Rock; Desert Botanical Garden / Las Noches de las Luminarias.\nSedona: Chapel of the Holy Cross, Bell Rock, Airport Scenic Lookout, Subway Cave / Boynton Canyon, Devil’s Bridge, the turquoise-arches McDonald’s and Tlaquepaque. Birthing Cave, Soldier Pass and Cathedral Rock are weather-and-energy alternatives.\nPetrified Forest National Park: Giant Logs, Crystal Forest, Blue Mesa, Newspaper Rock, Puerco Pueblo, Route 66 and Painted Desert.\nTucson / Green Valley: Saguaro National Park East and West, Arizona-Sonora Desert Museum and Titan Missile Museum.\nOptional: Goldfield Ghost Town. If northern Arizona has snow, replace Petrified Forest with another Sedona hiking day and head to Tucson earlier.",
    "itinerary": "Day 1|Arrive in the Phoenix area, collect the car and stay in Tempe / Scottsdale. Visit Dobbins Lookout for sunset if time allows; rest instead after a late flight.\nDay 2|Musical Instrument Museum 10:00–13:00; lunch, then optional Butterfly Wonderland 14:30–16:00. If Dobbins was missed on Day 1, try sunset around 16:30; otherwise walk and dine in Old Town Scottsdale. Recheck museum opening days for the chosen dates.\nDay 3|Early balloon trip in Glendale, about 3.5–4 hours. Scheduling it on the third day allows for arrival delays; ask about a next-morning rebooking if weather cancels it. Around 11:00 visit ASU Art Museum, then lunch and rest. Papago Park / Hole-in-the-Rock around 16:00; Las Noches de las Luminarias at Desert Botanical Garden in the evening, until about 21:00.\nDay 4|Check out around 09:00 and drive to Sedona. Chapel of the Holy Cross around 11:00, then lunch, check-in and Bell Rock. Sunset at Airport Scenic Lookout. If this is Christmas Eve, arrange dinner and buy food for Christmas Day ahead of time.\nDay 5|Start Boynton Canyon / Subway Cave early; allow 4–5 hours and use offline maps. The final spur lacks clear official signs. Stay on the main Boynton Canyon trail if the rock is icy. Rest or take a short red-rock outing in the afternoon; a place with a kitchen works well for Christmas Day.\nDay 6|Take Sedona Shuttle to Mescal / Dry Creek Vista for Devil’s Bridge; allow 3–4 hours. If the bridge is icy, enjoy the view from below. Visit the turquoise-arches McDonald’s and Tlaquepaque in the afternoon. Stay in Sedona.\nDay 7|Leave Sedona around 07:30 via Holbrook for Petrified Forest, entering south and exiting north: Rainbow Forest, Giant Logs, Crystal Forest, Blue Mesa, Newspaper Rock, Puerco Pueblo, Route 66 and Painted Desert. Leave before that year’s posted closing time; stay in Holbrook. If I-40 or park roads are icy, skip this section, choose a Sedona alternative and drive to Tucson that afternoon.\nDay 8|Holbrook to Tucson: about 4.5 hours of driving plus lunch and breaks. Depending on arrival and energy, drive Saguaro East’s Cactus Forest Drive, walk Mica View Trail or watch sunset. If already in Tucson after the weather backup, enjoy a relaxed full day at Saguaro East.\nDay 9|Check out around 08:30 for Green Valley. Aim for a 10:00 Titan Missile Museum underground tour, then see the surface exhibits. Leave around 12:15 for Arizona-Sonora Desert Museum, visiting 13:00–15:30. Add a short Saguaro West stop at Bajada Loop, Valley View Overlook or Signal Hill. Leave Tucson around 16:00–16:30 for Mesa / AZA and an airport-area hotel.\nDay 10|Plan checkout, refueling, car return and airport arrival around the eventual flight. Stay near the departure airport for an early flight and check after-hours car-return procedures.",
    "aurora": "Ballooning: The third morning leaves a buffer for flight delays and weather. Recheck participation requirements, duration and cancellation terms for the travel year.\nChristmas: Favor outdoor Sedona activities and rest on Christmas Day; buy food the day before. Recheck holiday museum hours and garden light dates.\nWinter backup: Choose cancellable Holbrook lodging. If snow affects I-40 or park roads, skip Petrified Forest and spend more time in Sedona or Tucson.\nTitan Missile Museum: Keep the underground tour and surface exhibits as an idea; later confirm opening, booking, stairs and accessibility.\nIf time is short: Drop Goldfield Ghost Town, Butterfly Wonderland, extra Sedona trails and Saguaro East first.",
